## How they work together — the full picture

```
Your pom.xml
│
├── <parent>  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│   └── spring-boot-starter-parent 3.4.1                              │
│       ├── Manages ALL dependency versions                            │
│       ├── Ensures compatible versions (no conflicts)                 │
│       └── Provides default settings                                  │
│                                                                      ▼
├── <dependencies>  ────────────── uses versions FROM parent ──► correct JARs downloaded
│   ├── spring-boot-starter-web                                        │
│   └── spring-boot-starter-test                                       │
│                                                                      ▼
└── <plugins>  ──────────────────────────────────────────────► runs during build
    └── spring-boot-maven-plugin
        ├── mvn spring-boot:run  → runs your app locally
        ├── mvn package          → creates fat JAR with all deps
        └── mvn clean install    → builds + installs to local .m2
```

---

## Where they play important roles

| Scenario | `<parent>` role | `<plugins>` role |
|---|---|---|
| **Creating project** | Sets up all versions automatically | Compiler plugin compiles your code |
| **Running locally** | Provides correct JAR versions | `spring-boot:run` starts the app |
| **Building for production** | Ensures all deps are compatible | Creates fat JAR for deployment |
| **Testing** | Provides JUnit versions | Surefire plugin runs tests |
| **Missing `<parent>`** | Version conflicts, missing JARs | Plugins can't find correct versions |
| **Missing plugin** | No effect on running | Can't run `mvn spring-boot:run` |

