## Your exact error — explained with this knowledge

```
NoClassDefFoundError: org/apache/commons/logging/LogFactory
         ↑
         commons-logging JAR was missing
         ↑
         because no <parent> in your pom.xml
         ↑
         Maven didn't know which version of
         commons-logging to download
         ↑
         so it downloaded NOTHING for logging
         ↑
         Spring Boot tried to use it → CRASH
```

> **One line summary:** `<parent>` = your **version manager** (what to download). `<plugins>` = your **build tools** (what to do with what's downloaded). Both are essential — parent without plugin means correct JARs but can't run. Plugin without parent means can run but wrong/missing JARs.